WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.830
His tenure as Tony Stark may have come to
an end, but the MCU has left Robert Downey

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.720
Jr. with the kind of professional resources
he'd never had before in his career, from

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.000
a massive worldwide fanbase to a hefty bank
account to the kind of clout in Hollywood

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.720
that will allow him to pursue a host of new
projects.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.220
Here's why he left the MCU, and what's ahead
for Marvel's first leading man.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.220
Getting off the MCU "bus"

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.780
First thing's first: Why did Downey and his
fellow Avenger Chris Evans elect to leave

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.369
the MCU in the first place?

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:26.500
Disney Twenty-Three magazine has the answer.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.250
In a recent chat with the insider outlet,
the iconic Iron Man actor said their time

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.590
was simply up, saying,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.700
"We had to get off.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.460
We opted to, and knew it was part of the job
to get off the bus while it rolled on to other

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.460
destinations.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.090
There’s something very sobering about it.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:42.530
I’m glad he and I will be there to welcome
others as they retire their jerseys."

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.910
"No amount of money ever bought a second of
time."

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.750
"Smart guy."

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.750
As for his legacy in the MCU, RDJ was his
usual charming and self-effacing self, saying,

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.460
"I really don’t need to look any farther
than my co-stars.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.680
Mark Ruffalo is an activist, Chris Evans is
a diehard American and proponent of true democracy.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.540
I don’t really have the gumption, the skill
set, the drive, or the humility either of

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.540
those guys do."

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.389
His modesty is sweet, but MCU fans will always
love RDJ 3000, and will keep their fingers

00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:13.689
crossed for a cameo or two as the Marvel machine
moves on without him.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:14.689
The Voyage of Doctor Dolittle

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:18.899
Two major film adaptations of Hugh Lofting's
Doctor Dolittle novels have already been released,

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:21.750
including Eddie Murphy's famously broad take
on the character.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.649
Now it's Downey's turn to take on the role
of an eccentric animal expert who's able to

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:27.369
talk to his animal friends.

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:31.670
Downey has been attached to the project since
the spring of 2017, and principal photography

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:35.469
on the film began the following year, but
then the production hit a snag.

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:40.149
In April of 2019, it was reported that producers
had serious concerns about the initial cut

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:41.149
of the film.

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:44.609
After some rewrites and much reported tweaking,
the studio pushed back the film's release

00:01:44.609 --> 00:01:47.502
date from summer 2019 to January 17, 2020.

00:01:47.502 --> 00:01:53.150
In addition to Downey in the title role, The
Voyage of Doctor Dolittle will feature an

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:57.479
all-star cast of celebrity voices for animals,
including Spider-Man himself, Tom Holland.

00:01:57.479 --> 00:01:58.479
Sherlock Holmes 3

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:02.679
Shortly after he began his cinematic journey
as Tony Stark, Robert Downey Jr. took on another

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:05.090
iconic character: Sherlock Holmes.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.890
Downey played the legendary detective in two
action-heavy films in 2009 and 2011, which

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.890
grossed more than $1 billion worldwide combined.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.040
The Sherlock Holmes films were directed by
Guy Ritchie and packed top-tier talent into

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.680
their casts, including Jude Law as Dr. Watson.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.920
In the spring of 2018, Warner Bros.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.540
Pictures finally announced a third film in
the series featuring the return of Downey

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.790
in the title role and Law as Watson.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.650
We know very little about the film, which
was originally set to be released on Christmas

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.069
Day, 2020, but has since been pushed back
to December 21, 2021.

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:40.069
This new date places the sequel's release
ten years after its predecessor, Sherlock

00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:41.599
Holmes: A Game of Shadows.

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:45.129
The project does not yet have an announced
director, which means there's a chance Ritchie

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:46.170
could also return.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.629
Dr. John Brinkley biopic

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:51.250
In 2017, it was announced that Downey would
star in an upcoming film based on an episode

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.280
of the Reply All podcast.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.450
The episode, titled "Man of the People," was
the story of John Brinkley, a doctor who rose

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:02.019
to fame and fortune in the early 20th century
for a number of strange and controversial

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:05.930
"medical" procedures, including transplanting
goat testicles into humans.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.980
As dramatized in the 2016 Brinkley documentary
Nuts!, the pioneering doc used radio as a

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.540
way to reach the masses.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.730
Downey will reportedly star in the film as
Brinkley, putting him in a great position

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.150
to use his charm onscreen for a conman role.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.939
Richard Linklater will direct, while Downey
and his wife Susan will produce through their

00:03:21.939 --> 00:03:23.560
Team Downey production banner.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.489
The film does not yet have a release date.

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:26.489
All-Star Weekend

00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:29.790
Downey has great comedy chops, something we've
known about him since the early days of his

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.629
career when he was playing supporting roles
in John Hughes films like Weird Science.

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:35.519
"This is Max.

00:03:35.519 --> 00:03:40.080
We call him Mad Max."

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.879
He's gotten more recent opportunities to show
off those skills thanks to films like Chef

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:44.889
and Due Date.

00:03:44.889 --> 00:03:48.629
Sometime soon, he'll be flexing his comedy
muscles in a big way yet again with a role

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:53.629
in All-Star Weekend, the directorial debut
of his The Soloist co-star Jamie Foxx.

00:03:53.629 --> 00:03:57.230
Foxx is the writer, director, and star of
the film, which follows two friends as they

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:01.129
try to make it from their home in Indiana
to the NBA All-Star Game in Los Angeles while

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:05.819
constantly battling each other as fans of
LeBron James and Steph Curry, respectively.

00:04:05.819 --> 00:04:10.209
All-Star Weekend does not have an announced
release date yet, and as of late 2018, Foxx

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:12.609
was still looking for the right distributor
for the project.

00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:13.609
Perry Mason

00:04:13.609 --> 00:04:18.380
Back in 2016 it was reported that Downey would
star in a new miniseries from HBO following

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:23.100
a reimagined version of criminal defense attorney
Perry Mason from the CBS television series

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.790
starring Raymond Burr which ran from 1957
to 1966.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.310
"You didn't kill Thompson.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.349
But you did, Mr Wells!"

00:04:31.349 --> 00:04:32.349
"Yes!

00:04:32.349 --> 00:04:35.530
I killed Ned Thompson!"

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:40.630
Set in 1930s Los Angeles, the miniseries is
set to focus on the character's origin story.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:44.330
When the project was initially announced,
True Detective creator Nic Pizzolatto was

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.500
also onboard to write the miniseries.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.970
Things have changed significantly in the last
three years, but Perry Mason is still happening.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:54.710
Downey is still very much involved, though
he will no longer star in the series.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:58.479
Downey has instead stepped back into the role
of executive producer on the series alongside

00:04:58.479 --> 00:05:00.600
his wife and producing partner Susan Downey.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:04.710
The Americans star Matthew Rhys has instead
been cast in the title role.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:05.710
The Footprint Coalition

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:09.060
He may be done playing Tony Stark, but Robert
Downey Jr.'s journey as a world-changing mogul

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.699
may be just beginning.

00:05:10.699 --> 00:05:15.490
Downey appeared at Amazon's ReMARS conference
in June 2019 and, in the midst of a 20-minute

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.520
talk about his life, career, and interest
in technology and the environment, he announced

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:20.710
a major new initiative.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.389
In April of 2020 Downey will launch the Footprint
Coalition, an organization that will work

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:29.300
to improve the environment using advanced
technologies like artificial intelligence

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.530
and nanotechnology.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.319
Basically, Downey is playing Tony Stark in
real life.

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:34.450
He said during the announcement,

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:38.849
"Between robots and nanotechnology, we could
clean up the planet significantly, if not

00:05:38.849 --> 00:05:40.440
totally, in 10 years."

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:44.349
At this point we still don't know exactly
what the Footprint Coalition will do first,

00:05:44.349 --> 00:05:46.699
or what technologies it will use to achieve
its goals.

00:05:46.699 --> 00:05:50.349
At the moment, the organization is little
more than a sparse website with an option

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.000
to sign up for a newsletter.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.720
But if RDJ is involved, it's likely to make
plenty of headlines in the years to come.

